{"slug":"numbers-starter-l5","artistFeel":"Ricky Martin","beat":"Uplifting Upbeat","data":{"title":"Numbers — Starter · Lesson 5","subject":"numbers","subjectLabel":"Numbers","level":"starter","lesson":5,"totalLessons":20,"genre":"Latin","lyrics":"[Intro]\n¡Vamos!\n\n[Hook]\nOne, two, three… Uno, dos, tres\nFour, five, six… Cuatro, cinco, seis\nCome count with me again.\n\n[Verse]\nBusy market, people all around,\nlearning numbers, listen to the sound.\nHalf… Mitad\nof the apples in my hand.\nTriple… Triple\nthe price, I understand.\n\nFifteen… Quince\noranges in the crate.\nTenfold… Décuplo\nthe fun, let's celebrate.\n\n[Hook]\nOne, two, three… Uno, dos, tres\nFour, five, six… Cuatro, cinco, seis\nCome count with me again.\n\n[Verse]\nLook at the scales, they weigh with care,\nQuintuple… Quíntuple\nthe weight, that's quite a pair.\nOne-tenth… Décima parte\nof the mangoes, let's divide.\nOne-twentieth… Vigésima parte\nof the grapes, side by side.\n\nIn the crowd, we find our way,\nHundredth… Centésima parte\nof the spices on display.\nThousandth… Milésima parte\nof the saffron, so fine.\nNumbers in Spanish, keeping in line.\n\n[Bridge]\nFrom the market, we wander through,\nVigésima parte\nof the stalls, a perfect view.\nUno, dos, tres\nwe count the steps we take.","vocab":[{"es":"mitad","en":"half"},{"es":"décuplo","en":"tenfold"},{"es":"triple","en":"triple"},{"es":"cuádruple","en":"quadruple"},{"es":"décima","en":"tenth"},{"es":"vigésima","en":"twentieth"},{"es":"centésima","en":"hundredth"},{"es":"milésima","en":"thousandth"},{"es":"décima parte","en":"one-tenth"},{"es":"vigésima parte","en":"one-twentieth"},{"es":"centésima parte","en":"one-hundredth"},{"es":"milésima parte","en":"one-thousandth"},{"es":"décima parte de","en":"tenth of"},{"es":"vigésima parte de","en":"twentieth of"},{"es":"centésima parte de","en":"hundredth of"}]},"timings":[{"start":0.079,"end":0.621,"loss":12.113259451729911},{"start":0.62,"end":7.579,"loss":2.587363640467326},{"start":7.579